Subject: [PATCH 1181/3799] soh: rename func_809CC774 ->
 EnBubble_UpdateCollider

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: transforms the collider's model-space sphere into world space and scales its radius by the current expansion, then copies it to the second element.
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bubble/z_en_bubble.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bubble/z_en_bubble.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bubble/z_en_bubble.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bubble/z_en_bubble.c
index 114cb050a..da1a0f05e 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bubble/z_en_bubble.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Bubble/z_en_bubble.c
@@ -318,7 +318,8 @@ u32 EnBubble_DetectPop(EnBubble* this, PlayState* play) {
     return EnBubble_CheckAcHit(this);  // was func_809CC648 [LLM:HIGH]
 }
 
-void func_809CC774(EnBubble* this) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_809CC774: transforms the collider's model-space sphere into world space and scales its radius by the current expansion, then copies it to the second element.
+void EnBubble_UpdateCollider(EnBubble* this) {
     ColliderJntSphElementDim* dim;
     Vec3f src;
     Vec3f dest;
@@ -437,6 +438,6 @@ void EnBubble_Draw(Actor* thisx, PlayState* play) {
 
     if (this->actionFunc != EnBubble_Disappear) {
         this->actor.shape.shadowScale = (f32)((this->expansionWidth + 1.0f) * 0.2f);
-        func_809CC774(this);
+        EnBubble_UpdateCollider(this);  // was func_809CC774 [LLM:HIGH]
     }
 }
